# twenty_role

Reads an existing role in the authenticated workspace through Metadata GraphQL. It does not create, change, or delete roles.

Specify exactly one of `role_id` or `label`. Labels are case-sensitive and include all configured whitespace. A blank label, missing role, or duplicate match is an error. Use a UUID when labels are not unique. The computed `id` is the matching role's stable UUID.

The automation account needs the `ROLES` settings permission. Object-record access alone does not grant permission to list roles.

## Example usage

{{ tffile "examples/data-sources/twenty_role/data-source.tf" }}

For UUID lookup, replace `label` with `role_id = "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111"`, using an existing role UUID from your workspace.

## Permission values

The six global capability booleans and explicit `permission_flags` describe the server's role configuration. Global permissions can grant access beyond the explicit flag set. This is not a full effective-permission calculation; object and field restrictions are not exported.

Nullable descriptions and icons stay null. A null permission flag list stays null rather than becoming an empty set. Missing required role values or inconsistent flag ownership cause an error instead of silently reporting a denied permission as false.

